{"Title":"An Act relative to technical rescue services","BillNumber":"S2535","DocketNumber":"SD2755","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"WFT0","Name":"Walter F. Timilty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WFT0","ResponseDate":"2023-08-21T14:51:13.07"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"WFT0","Name":"Walter F. Timilty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WFT0","ResponseDate":"2023-08-21T14:51:13.07"},{"Id":"SGX1","Name":"Steven George Xiarhos","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SGX1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-18T13:22:05.0733333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2535/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Timilty, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2535) (subject to Joint Rule 12) of Walter F. Timilty for legislation relative to technical rescue services.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 2 of Chapter 22D of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out the word \"and\" in line 11.\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 2 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is further amended by striking out in lines 11, 12, 13, and 14 the words \"of hazardous materials under the charge of a director to be known as the director of hazardous materials, the director of hazardous materials shall administer the regional hazardous material response teams\" and inserting in place thereof, the following new language:- and a division of special operations under the charge of a director to be known as the director of special operations. The special operations division shall include hazardous materials emergency response teams and technical rescue emergency response teams.\r\n\tSECTION 3. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out in line 6 of subsection (a), the words \"each technical rescue region\" and inserting in place thereof the following new words:- the state fire marshal.\r\n\tSECTION 4. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out subsection (b) in its entirety and inserting the following new language:- \r\n\t(b) There is hereby established within the department a technical rescue coordinating council, which shall serve as an advisory board to the state fire marshal. Said board shall review the development of standards, rules, procedures, and regulations for technical rescue emergency response and cost recovery. The board shall consist of the secretary of public safety or a designee; the state fire marshal or a designee; and five members to be appointed by the governor, 2 of whom shall be members of the Fire Chief's Association of Massachusetts, Inc., 2 of whom shall be members of the Professional Fire Fighters of Massachusetts; and 1 of whom shall be selected from a list comprised of 1 nominee from each regional technical rescue team and selected by the team's leadership. The governor shall appoint members for a term of 3 years and any such member shall be eligible for reappointment. A person shall not receive compensation for service as a member of the council but may receive reimbursement for all expenses necessarily incurred in connection with the member's official duties.\r\n\tThe majority of the council shall constitute a quorum to conduct business but a lesser number may adjourn from time to time. The council shall biannually elect a chair and vice-chair from among its members. \r\n\tSECTION 5: Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking in line 32 of subsection (c), the word \"develop\" and inserting in its place, the following new language:- advise the state fire marshal on the development of.\r\n\tSECTION 6: Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out in line 36 of subsection (d), the word \"establish\" and inserting in its place, the following new language:- advise the state fire marshal on the establishment of.\r\n\tSECTION 7. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out subsection section (e) in its entirety and inserting the following new paragraphs:-\r\n\tThe department, acting through the division of special operations, administered by the state fire marshal or his designee, shall prepare and from time to time update a technical rescue response plan.\r\n\tThe department may, at the request of the local fire department or on its own authority, dispatch member departments of the technical rescue response plan a site in the commonwealth for the purpose of conducting a technical rescue response. During a technical rescue response, the team leader shall have complete operational authority for technical rescue emergency response team operations at all times. Once the team leader has determined that the imminent danger of the technical rescue incident has been satisfactorily mitigated, the team leader shall thereafter notify the incident commander. The incident commander shall have authority over the technical rescue response site during a technical rescue response.\r\n\tSECTION 8. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by adding the following new paragraph at the end of subsection (f):- Any technical rescue response action taken by a member department under the technical rescue response plan shall be deemed to have been taken on behalf of the department and for the benefit of the commonwealth for the purpose of implementing the provisions of this chapter.\r\n\tSECTION 9. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out in line 54 of subsection (g) the words \"the department of fire services, in consultation with the technical rescue coordinating council may promulgate,\" and inserting in place, the following new language:- the state fire marshal may promulgate rules and\r\n\tSECTION 10. Section 6 of Chapter 22D, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by adding the following new subsection:-\r\n\t(h) The commonwealth shall, subject to appropriation, reimburse a municipality for costs incurred for the technical rescue response of its qualified members of a technical rescue response team and shall pay an annual stipend of $5,000 to each qualified member of that team. \r\n\tQualification shall be established by the state fire marshal.\r\n\tSECTION 11. Section 2DDDDD of Chapter 29, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out in lines 2 and 3, the second sentence in its entirety. \r\n\tSECTION 12. Section 2DDDDD of Chapter 29, as so appearing, is hereby amended inserting in line 4 after the word \"contract\", the following new words:- for services or otherwise.\r\n\tSECTION 13. Section 2DDDDD of Chapter 29, as so appearing, is hereby amended by inserting in line 15 after the word \"expended\", the following new words:- by the state fire marshal, as head of the department of fire services, who shall act as administrator of the fund,\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Suspend Rules","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}